  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1231 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nPotential Near Surface Smoke Impacts Into Thursday:\n\nA stout area of anticyclonic flow over the Upper Mississippi \nRiver Valley will cause a mostly persistent forecast until \nFriday when precipitation chances increase from west to east. \nMain impact concern through midweek will be potential near \nsurface smoke causing poor air quality. Tuesday satellite \nimagery exhibited the off- surface increased vertically \nintegrated smoke over and upstream of the forecast area with the\nanticyclonic flow expected to sink particulates to the surface \nWednesday evening into the nighttime hours (HRRR 28.18Z). \nLocation of high pressure in relation to the local forecast area\nwill determine extent of local impacts with current confidence \nfor highest impacts primarily west of the Mississippi River \nValley.\n\nPrecipitation Chances Friday Into Saturday:\n\nA deepening extratropical cyclone will slide east-southeast \nthrough the Northern to Central Plains Thursday night through \nFriday, bringing precipitation chances across the Upper Midwest \nas it passes. Current confidence in the low's progression \njogging south as it approaches the Upper Mississippi River \nValley abates higher confidence for higher precipitation \nprobabilities and unstable air west and south of the local \nforecast area. Although, without this southern shunt, locally \nincreased rainfall amounts and instability is possible. While \noutlying, select EPS members suggests 3\"+ QPF in select local \nareas with a more northern, moist solution.\n\nCurrent long term global ensemble confidence keeps the near \nnormal low level temperatures over the forecast area until early\nnext week when low level theta e advection ramps up.",
